      "writtenOn": "2021-12-20T12:08:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s return it instead of mutating it. This will simplify your code because you can make mMatchRule final and you won\u0027t have to pass the includeWildcard argument to assertRequestableMatchRule ; instead you\u0027ll pass the deduced rule to assertRequestableParameters which is easier to understand.\n\nThere are also other reasons it\u0027s a poor idea to mutate it :\n• It\u0027s hard for readers to understand the flow in assertRequestableParameters because a reader needs to understand that the member has been mutated first.\n• It would make it very hard to create a copy constructor for the builder, which is something we sometimes do",
